==Trivia==
===General===
*The puns, references and alliterations that comprise most of the Meow Medals' names are specific to the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]]; the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese]], Taiwanese and Korean versions go with a much more formal naming scheme, simply using the name of the associated character or stage without any attempt at cleverness. For example, the [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]]' Meow Medals just use the names of the units: ''Forest Child'' is called ''Ururun'', ''Tiny Nemesis'' is called ''Nyandam'', and so on.
**In BCJP, most of the [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone Stages]]' Meow Medals are named after the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s themselves, but strangely use kanji instead of katakana for their prefixes. For example, the ''Dark Skies'' Medal is called 暗黒サイクロン ("Darkness Cyclone") rather than [[Dark Cyclone]]'s Japanese name, ブラックサイクロン (literally "Black Cyclone"). Exceptions include ''Red Horizon'' (entirely katakana, just like [[Red Cyclone]]'s Japanese name) and ''Typhoon Z'' (''Z Cyclone'', whereas [[Zyclone]]'s Japanese name is Undead Cyclone).
*The text on the ''World of Darkness'' Meow Medal is the Japanese word 魔界 ''makai'' ("Demon World" or "Devil World") written in upside-down katakana.
*Since the Japanese version of [[Empire of Cats]] only takes place in Japan instead of the whole world, BCJP has different icons for the ''Builder of Empires'', ''Undead Slayer'' and ''World of Darkness'' Meow Medals.
**Moreover, since BCJP only has one set of chapters taking place across the world, the ''The Future is Ours'' and ''...And Stay Dead'' Meow Medals lack the UFOs that are present in the English Version, where they are needed to make them distinguishable from the English Empire of Cats Medals.
*Prior to the addition of Legend Helpers in the [[Version 10.4 Update]], ''May I Assist You?''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s description was, "Recruit a top-class [[Gamatoto Expedition|Gamatoto]] helper."
*Prior to the reworking of difficulty systems in the [[Version 10.7 Update]], the ''I Am Legend'' Meow Medals' descriptions were "Clear all # ★ [[Stories of Legend]] maps."
*When [[Attack of the Omens]] was added in [[Version 12.2 Update|Version 12.2]], it lacked a Meow Medal unlike the other Colossus [[Gauntlet]]s. The Medal was later added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]].
*''Omens'' is the only Colossus Gauntlet Medal whose description is not phrased as "Clear (event name)", instead being "Clear the "Omens" Gauntlet Map".
*''Lord Luza'' is the only Meow Medal to show a Legend Cat's [[True Form]] rather than its Normal Form, most likely because [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N000]] is indistinguishable from the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]].

===References===
*The ''I Am Legend'' Meow Medals reference the [[wikipedia:I Am Legend (novel)|1954 post-apocalypse novel]] of the same name.
*''Charon's Crossing'' is a reference to Greek mythology, in which [[wikipedia:Charon|Charon]] is the ferryman of the underworld who transports souls across the rivers [[wikipedia:Styx|Styx]] and [[wikipedia:Archeron|Acheron]].
*''Lock the Gates'' refers to the fallen gate [[wikipedia:Rajōmon|Rashōmon]], which is the namesake of the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] that must be cleared in order to unlock the Medal.
*''Sanzu Swamp Guardian'' is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Sanzu River|Sanzu River]], a river in Japanese Buddhist tradition which the souls of the deceased must cross before they can reach the afterlife.
*''Holidays in the Sun'' may be a reference to the song of the same name by the [[wikipedia:Sex Pistols|Sex Pistols]], especially since the [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]] stages' Japanese names are also references to songs.
*''Baron Wasted'' may be a reference to Baron Wasteland, a character from the game show ''[[wikipedia:Where in Time Is Carmen Sandiego? (game show)|Where in Time Is Carmen Sandiego?]]''.
*''Who You Gonna Call?'' is a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Ghostbusters|Ghostbusters]]''.
*''Buns of Steel'' is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Greg Smithey|series of exercise videos]] of the same name from the 80s and 90s.

===Errors===
*The ''Builder of Empires'', ''The Future is Ours'' and ''Cosmos Conquistador'' Medals' descriptions say Gold [[Treasure]]s where they should say Superior Treasures.
*The ''I Am Legend'' Medals' descriptions say [[Legend Stages]] despite only needing [[Stories of Legend]] to be cleared. This appears to be a localization error: in Japanese, Legend Stages and Stories of Legend share the name Legend Story (レジェンドストーリー), so the localizers may not have realized which it was referring to.
*[[Uncanny Legends]] is not pluralized in the ''I Am Uncanny Legend'' Medals' descriptions.
*Prior to [[Version 11.4 Update|Version 11.4]], ''The Big Z''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s description said [[Daboo of the Dead]] instead of [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Dead on Debut]].
*''Another Year''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s description refers to [[Happy New Year? (Monthly Event)|Happy New Year?]] as Happy New Year...?.
*The "be" in [[Bears be Bare (Monthly Event)|Bears be Bare]] is capitalized in ''Unbearable''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s description.
*''Vox Deus'' is grammatically incorrect. If referring to [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]], it should instead say ''Vox Deae'' which translates to "the voice of a goddess." If it is referring to some other unknown deity, it should instead be ''Vox Dei.''
*''Making Money'', ''Making Money 2'', ''Nouveau Riche'', ''Nouveau Riche 2'', ''One Percenter'' and ''One Percenter 2'' are ironically unlocked by spending cents, not earning them.

